  - Scholar is the book''s category name; the catalog files those skills under Technical and Science, so that pick spans both.
  - xp_table is this class''s OWN ladder, the "Gosai Assassin R.C.C." column on printed 215 (render p216), lower bounds 0, 2,151, 4,301, 9,601, 18,201, 28,401, 38,601, 54,801, 75,201, 100,401, 132,601, 185,801, 240,201, 295,401, 365,601 (level 15 runs to 425,800). It is not the Assassin''s ladder. No misprints in the column.
  - Hand to Hand: Skudasa, printed 45, level table as printed: 1 two attacks per melee and +2 strike; 2 +3 parry and dodge, +2 pull punch, +2 roll with punch/fall; 3 all kick attacks; 4 +1 attack and +1 initiative; 5 claws 3D6 and pop kick 5D6; 6 critical strike on an unmodified 17-20; 7 hand and foot claws as paired weapons, and may parry swords and other hand held weapons; 8 leap attack, +1 initiative, +2 pull punch; 9 +1 attack; 10 +2 parry and dodge; 11 body throw/flip, +1 initiative; 12 death blow on an unmodified 20; 13 +2 damage; 14 +1 attack; 15 +2 strike and disarm. The catalog''s Hand to Hand: Skudasa skill row carries the same fifteen levels.
  - category occ with race_restrictions only gosai: the book calls it an R.C.C., and it is an occupation only a Gosai takes. occ_group men-of-arms and men_of_arms true because it is the Assassin O.C.C., which the main book prints among the Men of Arms; it states no S.D.C. of its own.
  - tags: evil is carried from the Assassin O.C.C. (anarchist or evil only), which this entry does not change; the Gosai race line on the same page reads "Any, but usually selfish or aberrant evil" and is about the race.
  - Equipment is the Assassin''s without the two daggers, the three weapons of choice and the studded leather. The weapons go because the entry says he uses none. The studded leather is dropped by INFERENCE from the metal allergy on printed 44; this entry states no armor rule.
  - This entry prints no money or equipment line; both are the Assassin''s.
  - restrictions carries the production assassin row''s armor-penalty line and its thieves-guild-services line. That row''s weapon-quality line (every starting weapon a basic S.D.C. weapon of very good quality) was dropped because the class uses no weapons. The armor line''s opening clause about starting in studded leather is not repeated, since the studded leather is left out of the equipment.
